A cycle (a <-> b) and a node (z) that depends on a but is not part of the
cycle. The sort must break the cycle with an edge inside it and keep z's
edge, so z comes after a.

  $ for m in a b z; do
  >   case $m in
  >     a) ref=B;; b) ref=A;; z) ref=A;;
  >   esac
  >   printf '[@@@css ".%s{color:red;}"]\nlet _ = %s.x\n' $m $ref > $m.ml
  > done

  $ styled-ppx.generate a.ml b.ml z.ml
  styled-ppx: dependency cycle among a.ml, b.ml; dropping the edge from b.ml to a.ml to keep a deterministic order
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  .b{color:red;}
  .a{color:red;}
  .z{color:red;}
